==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Verbena the Bride''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Opulent Verbena''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
She can be quite useful when dealing with [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies. Even if she does low damage, she can kill many Metal enemies with one Critical Hit (however, her first attack isn't strong enough to OHKO [[Super Metal Hippoe]]). However, it isn't recommended to use Verbena against anything that isn't Metal.

Despite having short range, Verbena actually outranges most of the Metal enemies, which gives her more usage against them and makes her extremely useful in stages like [[Utopia is Over There]], where most enemies are Metal enemies. However, since her attacks increase in strength, this can be rather troubling, since her first hit can't kill Super Metal Hippoe in one Crit, and a Critical Hit from her third hit is the only one that can OHKO a 100% [[Sir Metal Seal]].

She approximately has a 38.6% chance of getting at least 1 critical hit in her multi-hit attack, which is increased to 57.8% in her True Form. She can also form a synergy with [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]. While Hayabusa hits Metal enemies that are far away, Verbena can hit those that reach his blind spot.

==='''Talents'''===
The first talent that Verbena gets is an increase to her Critical Hit chance, from 25% to 35% per hit. The Multi-hit brings her overall Crit odds to aproximately 72.5% per attack cycle compared to her usual 57.8%. Her Critical talent simply give her a better chance to crit and to be a better critter for those who want a good upgrade for Verbena. [[Survive]] gives Verbena one more opportunity to reposition, which can be helpful on occasion. However, at the steep cost of '''235''' NP, this should hardly be seriously considered, especially when its only use case is to be extra assurance during emergencies. [[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Freeze]] should be avoided, since there is hardly any stages for this to find proper applicability; Even for stages like [[Electric Bath]], it doesn't carry its weight enough to justify investing into. Attack Buff and HP Buff are not particularly useful, since Verbena dependant on neither damage nor HP. If you need her to be tankier, or to deal more damage, it would be far better to use [[Catseye]]s before NP.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
A one-slot small Attack Up [[Cat Combo]] might sound alluring, but it isn't particularly practical outside of specific circumstances. The space efficiency is the only thing this Cat Combo has going for it, as the unit associated with it, Verbena, is underwhelming across the board and will almost always be a dead slot in your lineup. When compared to other readily available two-slot Attack Up Cat Combos like [[Tiny Ancient Hunt (Combo)|Tiny Ancient Hunt]], [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]], and even [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]], they all feature at least one noteworthy unit who can almost guarantee some amount of value from being deployed. Whether it's [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]], [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]], [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]], or [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]], these units all bring a very powerful generalist element to the table. Truthfully, this Cat Combo's main benefits come in the form of combo stacking, where its space efficiency can provide you with unique Cat Combo combinations, such as a 25% attack buff for only three slots (骨まで愛して, Land Air Assault), thus giving way to things like a 25% Attack Buff + 30% Strengthen (骨まで愛して, Land-Air Assault, [[Cosplay Fans (Combo)|Cosplay Fans]]). [[Catclaw Dojo]] is where you will see this advantage pay dividends as it gives way to more flexible lineups and higher overall potentials. If you have the spare [[Catseye|Dark Catseyes]] and nothing better to spend them on, this Ultra Talent provides something nothing else can. Otherwise, you're free to disregard it.

'''[[Surge Attack]]''' grants her pierce, though its damage varies greatly depending on the Multi-Hit. Accounting for Critical Hits and with all other noteworthy damage buffing Talents, you can expect an average DPS of ~9.5k, which is still relatively low for the NP investment required for this unit. Granted, the only reason you would consider getting this to begin with is likely because you already have her Cat Combo unlocked. If you actually plan on using Verbena as an anti-Metal, then this Ultra Talent is a bang for your buck as it effectively doubles her DPS.

'''HP Buff+''' is on the same boat as Surge Attack. As a midranger, she's very prone to taking sucker punches as she's dishing damage out, and this Ultra Talent just lets her handle the punishment a little better. It's only 100 NP, so if you're at the point of investing into Verbena, you could honestly get this before the regular Defense Buff.

